      "content": "it's not just a single piece of info though. i've been careful. the common thread isn't my username, it's the timing and how \"clean\" the removals are. there's no \"suspicious activity\" warning, no \"password reset\" notifications, just... nothingness. it's like the accounts never existed. \n\nit makes me wonder if this is even about a data breach. if a \"Shadow Admin\" or some kind of centralized entity wanted to make someone disappear from the web, they wouldn't just steal a password, they'd just revoke the identity entirely. looking at the \"pattern\" you mentioned, it's not a pattern of errors, it's a pattern of deletions. can you look for any documented ways a singular high-level actor could bypass individual platform security to execute a wide-scale identity erasure?",
